Original commit body from 0d8f301f6e3d770a2c5df9589660ca639daed4b8:

IoPrimitive.kind -- the catalogue's functions:/methods:/attributes: --
had no stated meaning, and the catalogues' own notes gave three rules:
what the callee IS (rust), whether a value supplies its owner (cpp,
scala, python), and what the language's analyzer stamps (java, kotlin).
Every consumer that branches on the value needs the second. Axiom as
ratified by the owner (INV-zikab, after a three-seat panel):

  A row's kind says how the primitive is reached from the row's own
  module: method iff called on an INSTANCE of module; function iff
  called on module itself (namespace, package, type, companion object,
  named global) or with no owner; attribute iff read, not called.

The four ADR-0024 artifacts:
- registry + predicates: hypergumbo_core.io_primitive_kinds
  (reached_through_an_instance / called_on_a_named_owner /
  read_not_called, KIND_* constants, kind_for_yaml_section);
- consumer pattern: the 18 literal sites in io_boundary, verify_claims,
  analyzer_disclosure and taint now go through the predicates and
  constants, with no behaviour change;
- static enforcement: find_kind_literal_drift, run by
  scripts/check-io-boundary-drift (the pre-commit step that already
  covers IoPrimitive's boundary axis);
- runtime enforcement: tests/test_io_primitive_kinds.py -- every shipped
  row carries a registered kind; no name list sits under an unregistered
  key (a typo'd 'method:' used to vanish silently); the scanner fires on
  each offence shape; the Swift constructor-shape check.

io-primitive-kind is wired into _known_axes() and declared on
IoPrimitive.kind (was bounded-enum, with a docstring naming two of its
three values -- WI-fazad).

No row changes kind. The 91 shipped rows the axiom rejects sit in a
shrink-only ledger, each naming its blocker (INV-pimir, WI-kilap,
WI-narij, INV-gujoh, WI-ziviv); the test fails on a fixed or removed
entry and pins the size.

